## INCIDENT REPORT

Based on my analysis of the PCAP, I have identified a confirmed STRRAT (Remote Access Trojan) infection on a Windows 11 enterprise workstation. The malware was actively beaconing to its command-and-control server during the capture window.

```json
{
  "victim": {
    "ip": "172.16.1.66",
    "mac": "00:1e:64:ec:f3:08",
    "hostname": "DESKTOP-SKBR25F",
    "user": "ccollier"
  },
  "malware_family": "STRRAT",
  "attribution_confidence": "signature-confirmed",
  "iocs": [
    {
      "type": "c2_endpoint",
      "value": "141.98.10.79:12132",
      "evidence": "206 TCP packets from victim to this endpoint on odd port 12132, no TLS handshake. Payload contains unencrypted pipe-delimited beaconing data with literal 'STRRAT' identifier, bot ID '1BE8292C', and exfiltrated system information. Beaconing interval ~5 seconds (frames 9066-10734). Classic STRRAT C2 signature."
    },
    {
      "type": "file_name",
      "value": "STRRAT bot ID 1BE8292C",
      "evidence": "Unique identifier observed in beacon payload: 'ping|STRRAT|1BE8292C|DESKTOP-SKBR25F|ccollier|Microsoft Windows 11 Pro|64-bit|Windows Defender||1.6|US:United States|Not Installed|1 Sec' (hex: 70696e677c5354525241547c31424538323932437c...)"
    }
  ],
  "benign_context": [
    {
      "type": "cdn_ip",
      "value": "199.232.196.209",
      "evidence": "Fastly CDN (repo1.maven.org), 455 packets on 443. Legitimate software update traffic."
    },
    {
      "type": "cdn_ip",
      "value": "185.199.110.133",
      "evidence": "GitHub CDN (objects.githubusercontent.com), 71 packets on 443. Legitimate source code/object download."
    },
    {
      "type": "internal_host",
      "value": "172.16.1.4",
      "evidence": "Domain controller (WIRESHARK-WS-DC). Benign internal directory services traffic (LDAP, Kerberos, DNS, SMB)."
    }
  ],
  "incident_summary": "Windows 11 workstation 172.16.1.66 (user: ccollier) is infected with STRRAT, a Java-based remote access trojan. The malware is actively beaconing to C2 server 141.98.10.79:12132 every 5 seconds with system telemetry, including OS version, Windows Defender status, and geographic location. Malware version 1.6 is confirmed via beacon payload. No file transfer or command activity observed in this capture window; only passive reconnaissance beaconing."
}
```

**Key Findings:**

- **Malware Confirmation:** The literal string "STRRAT" appears in the unencrypted TCP beaconing payload, providing definitive signature confirmation.
- **C2 Beaconing Pattern:** 206 packets sent to 141.98.10.79:12132 at 5-second intervals with exfiltrated system information (hostname, user, Windows version, defender status, geolocation).
- **Bot ID:** Unique identifier 1BE8292C observed in all beacon payloads, allowing for cross-reference in threat intelligence databases.
- **No Active Command Response:** The C2 server sends only ACKs; no command payloads observed during the capture window. The infection appears to be in a passive beaconing state.
